# The 1983 source: at the end of a text file that RUN name loads, INCHR's NOTCHN runs the program at once (RUNC, NEWSTT), so a last line with no CR, still in BUF, isn't entered; PC-BASIC enters it first. (LOAD's own end, not run, ends the line with a CR: it is entered.)
Ok
OPEN "O",#1,"LD.BAS":PRINT #1,"10 PRINT 1"
Ok
PRINT #1,"PRINT 2":PRINT #1,"20 PRINT 3":CLOSE
Ok
LOAD "LD"
Direct statement in file
Ok
LIST
10 PRINT 1
